Root cause found: the lock descriptor is opened without `O_BINARY`. On Windows the CRT translates the trailing `\n` to `\r\n`; `fstat()` reports physical bytes while `os.read()` returns translated logical bytes, so the size-bounded witness reader asks for one byte too many and returns `None`. I’m adding a regression that requires binary descriptor mode before applying the production fix.
